{title: For the Beauty of the Earth}
{artist: Folliott Pierpoint}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 92}

Verse 1
[F]For the beauty [C]of the earth, [F]for the glory [C]of the skies,
[F]for the love which [Bb]from our birth [F]over and a[C]round us lies:

Chorus
[F]Lord of all, to [Bb]thee we raise
[F]this our hymn of [C]grateful [F]praise.

Verse 2
[F]For the beauty of each [C]hour, Of the day and [F]of the night, Hill and [C]vale, and tree and flow'r,
[F]Sun and moon, and stars of light. [Bb]Lord of all, to Thee [F]we raise, This our hymn of grateful praise.

Verse 3
[F]For the joy of [C]ear and eye, For the [F]heart and mind's delight, For [C]the mystic harmony Linking
[F]sense to sound and sight. Lord [Bb]of all, to Thee [F]we raise, This our hymn of grateful praise.

Verse 4
[F]For the joy of [C]human love, Brother, sister, [F]parent, child, Friends on earth [C]and friends above, For
[F]all gentle thoughts and mild. Lord [Bb]of all, to Thee [F]we raise, This our hymn of grateful praise.

Verse 5
[F]For Thy Church, that [C]evermore Lifteth holy hands [F]above, Off'ring up on [C]every shore Her pure
[F]sacrifice of love. Lord of [Bb]all, to Thee we [F]raise, This our hymn of grateful praise.
